Alembic migrations for the ScrollKiller scoreboard API.

Async single-database configuration (asyncpg).

⚑ These run on the DIRECT Neon endpoint, never the pooled one. `env.py` reads
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT and refuses to run without it — it does NOT fall back to
DATABASE_URL. The reasoning is in that file's docstring and in D62; the short
version is that Alembic's version lock is connection-scoped and a transaction
pooler does not preserve it.

    # review the SQL without touching anything
    DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=postgresql+asyncpg://... alembic upgrade head --sql

    # actually apply it
    DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=postgresql+asyncpg://... alembic upgrade head

    # new revision (autogenerate needs a reachable database)
    DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=postgresql+asyncpg://... alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"

Two things autogenerate will not do for you:

1. Wrap constraint names in `op.f()`. Alembic re-applies the naming convention
   from `Base.metadata` to names in a revision, so a plain
   `name="ck_daily_counts_count_non_negative"` comes back out as
   `ck_daily_counts_ck_daily_counts_count_non_negative`.
2. Extend the `platform` ENUM. Adding a member to `app.platforms.Platform` needs
   a revision running `ALTER TYPE platform ADD VALUE ...`, and on older Postgres
   that cannot run inside a transaction.

Do not import `app.models` into a revision. A migration is a historical fact and
must not change meaning when the models do; `tests/test_migrations.py` is what
keeps the two from drifting apart.
